// Package i3 is the i3bar protocol as a family: a status line is a tree of
// `block`s under a `bar`, and the running program writes it to stdout every
// time the state it reads changes.
//
// DESIGN SKETCH -- this does not compile. It is written against the proposal
// in `example/i3blocks/README.md`, and every construct that does not exist yet
// is marked `PROPOSED` where it is used.
//
// Nothing here is a platform. The family is rendered by whichever host the
// build picks -- gtk4, fyne, a headless Go loop -- because what it generates
// is Go, not widgets: `block[go.language]` is a *language* override, and the host only
// has to give it a Model to hang fields on, a loop to post onto and a `main`
// to run before.
//
// The protocol, for reference (https://i3wm.org/docs/i3bar-protocol.html):
// a header line, `[`, then one JSON array of blocks per status line, each
// followed by a comma. With `click_events` set, i3bar writes an endless JSON
// array of click objects to stdin, each naming the block's `name` and
// `instance`.
